    "working_thesis": "Hannah Arendt's interpretation of the natural and the artificial in The Human Condition transforms the conventional cultural critique of modernity by subordinating ecological concerns to a political philosophy centered on human plurality, wherein re-naturalization and the dominance of the biological life process represent the ultimate threat to human freedom."
